{"author":{"id":"8022379585b4ab99ca8775db3eb67d33fcb256817114c28e51ccc1e9f55cdec4"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1792310691,"nonce":"uxtm6u5TgqbRd5uPLsjQFouVHME=","title":"FIXED (71bff00). RoPE convention bug — GGUF Llama models bake llama.cpp's GGML_ROPE_TYPE_NORMAL (interleaved consecutive pairs `(x[2i], ...","message":"`tools/llama-diff/layer-diff.sh \"Hello\"` invokes both\n`llama-eval-callback` (which dumps per-tensor `sum = N` for every op\nin the compute graph) and Rayzor's `DumpLayers.hx` (which walks\n`LlamaModel` printing the same milestones), joins on label, and\nreports relative error per row. Output before the fix:\n\n```\nembd                         1.140602       1.140603    0.00000   (match)\nattn_norm-0                 -1.507175      -1.507173    0.00000   (match)\nQcur-0                      46.449635      46.449692    0.00000   (match — pre-RoPE)\nQcur-0-rope                 65.534615      14.427881    0.78      \u003c-- DIFF\nKcur-0-rope                119.889374      99.578964    0.17      \u003c-- DIFF\nattn_out-0                   1.037153       0.973288    0.06      \u003c-- DIFF\n```\n\n`Qcur-0` (post the Q linear projection) matches perfectly, then\n`Qcur-0-rope` (after RoPE) is wildly off — pinpointed RoPE in two\nruns of the harness.\n\n\n`runtime/src/tensor.rs::rayzor_tensor_rope` was using **half-split**\npairing for the rotation:\n\n```rust\nlet off_lo = base + i;\nlet off_hi = base + i + half;\n```\n\nThat's correct for un-converted HF transformers tensors. But the\nGGUF that `unsloth/Llama-3.2-1B-Instruct-GGUF` ships was produced by\nthe HF-to-GGUF converter, which permutes the Q and K projection\nweights so the *interleaved* layout produces the same numerical\nresult. llama.cpp loads those weights and uses\n`GGML_ROPE_TYPE_NORMAL = 0` — which the cited `ggml_compute_forward_rope_f32`\nNORMAL branch pairs `i+0` with `i+1`. Confirmable directly:\n\n```\n$ llama-eval-callback -m model.gguf -p Hi -n 1 --temp 0 -lv 4 | grep -i rope\n  llama.rope.freq_base f32 = 500000.000000\n  llama.rope.dimension_count u32 = 64\n  print_info: rope type = 0          ← NORMAL = interleaved\n```\n\nThe fix is two lines:\n\n```rust\n// before (half-split, HF convention):\nlet off_lo = base + i;\nlet off_hi = base + i + half;\n// after (interleaved, GGUF/NORMAL convention):\nlet off_lo = base + 2 * i;\nlet off_hi = base + 2 * i + 1;\n```\n\n\n[[project-llama-chat-coherence-phase-c]] previously claimed Llama 3\nuses half-split because that's what `transformers/models/llama/modeling_llama.py::rotate_half`\ndoes. The note conflated *HF tensor layout* (half-split rotation on\nun-converted tensors) with *GGUF tensor layout* (interleaved rotation\non permuted-by-converter tensors). When that memory was written, the\nbmm-strides and reshape-materialise bugs dominated the user-visible\noutput, so switching from interleaved → half-split was a *partial*\ncorrection that masked the real bug behind a larger one. With those\ntwo fixed first, layer-diff isolated the RoPE convention.\n\nThe numbers in `tools/llama-diff/layer-diff.sh` win over the memory\nnote.\n\n\n```\nprompt: \"What is the capital of France?\"\n  llama.cpp: \"The capital of France is Paris.\"\n  rayzor   : \"The capital of France is Paris.\"\n\nprompt: \"Write a haiku about the moon\"\n  llama.cpp: \"Silver crescent glow / Luna's gentle, peaceful face /\n              Midnight's soft delight\"\n  rayzor   : \"Here is a haiku about the moon: Silver crescent glow /\n              Luna's gentle, peaceful face / Midnight's soft delight\"\n\nprompt: \"What is 2 + 2?\"\n  llama.cpp: \"2 + 2 equals 4.\"\n  rayzor   : \"2 + 2 = 4\"\n```\n\n128/128 haxe + 709 lib + tiny-transformer all green.\n\n\n- Layer 15 still shows divergence because llama.cpp's last-layer FFN\n  only computes the last row (prefill optimisation) while DumpLayers\n  computes the full sequence. Cosmetic for the diff harness; doesn't\n  affect inference correctness.\n- The harness should also dump and diff the final-token sampled\n  argmax id, not just sums.\n- `nue.sampling.TemperatureSampler` import-cascade SIGILL still\n  unsolved (workaround: inline `LocalTempSampler` in Main.hx).\n\n\n- [[project-llama-chat-coherence-phase-c]] — previous coherence\n  pass. The bmm-stride and reshape-materialise fixes here were\n  correct; the half-split RoPE note was wrong.\n- `tools/llama-diff/` — the harness that found this. Reuse for any\n  future suspected forward-pass divergence.\n\n---\nArchived from Claude memory `bugs_rope_interleaved_for_gguf` on 2026-10-18. A record of past work; open items in it may have their own issues.","files":null}]}